.TH io_uring_register_spare 3 "October 23, 2026" "liburing-2.17" "liburing Manual"
.SH NAME
io_uring_register_spare, io_uring_unregister_spare, io_uring_register_spare_debug \- manage a SpareRing executor group
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <liburing.h>
.PP
.BI "int io_uring_register_spare(struct io_uring *" ring ","
.BI "                            struct io_uring_spare_reg *" reg ");"
.PP
.BI "int io_uring_unregister_spare(struct io_uring *" ring ");"
.PP
.BI "int io_uring_register_spare_debug(struct io_uring *" ring ","
.BI "                                  struct io_uring_spare_debug *" dbg ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
SpareRing v5.14 is a research prototype and is not part of upstream Linux.
These functions require a kernel implementing the prototype.
.PP
.BR io_uring_register_spare (3)
attaches
.I ring
to a group of spare executors. Eligible runs of SQEs can be delegated to
these executors. With the pull feature enabled, an executor may lease the
SQ and consume eligible SQEs after the application publishes them. The
submitting task takes over when necessary, preserving the ring's
.B IORING_SETUP_DEFER_TASKRUN
completion discipline.
.PP
The argument pointed to by
.I reg
has the following layout:
.PP
.in +4n
.EX
struct io_uring_spare_reg {
	__s32	attach_fd;
	__u32	nr_exec;
	__u32	n_max;
	__u32	u_pending;
	__u32	u_chunks;
	__u32	linger_us;
	__u32	mode;
	__u32	flags;
	__u64	cpumask;
	__u32	cpumask_len;
	__u32	n_min;
	__u32	rescue_us;
	__u32	features;
};
.EE
.in
.TP
.I attach_fd
Set to -1 to create a new executor group. Otherwise, this must be a file
descriptor for an io_uring instance already attached to a group. The group
must belong to the caller's thread group; joining a group from another
thread group fails with
.BR -EPERM .
.TP
.I nr_exec
Number of executors to create for a new group, from 1 through 64.
This field is used only when creating a group.
.TP
.I n_max
Maximum number of SQEs in a delegated chunk or pull unit. Zero selects
the default of 32; the maximum is 64.
.TP
.I u_pending
Maximum number of unclaimed push chunks for this ring. Zero selects the
default of 4.
.TP
.I u_chunks
Maximum number of outstanding chunks, including unclaimed and claimed
chunks, for this ring. Zero selects the default of 16.
.TP
.I linger_us
Time in microseconds that an executor polls for work before sleeping. Zero
selects the default of 50; the maximum is 1000.
.TP
.I mode
One of the modes described below.
.TP
.I flags
Bitwise OR of the flags described below.
.TP
.I cpumask
User address of a CPU bitmap for a new executor group, stored in a
64-bit integer. Zero allows any CPU. This field is used only when
creating a group.
.TP
.I cpumask_len
Size in bytes of the bitmap pointed to by
.IR cpumask .
.TP
.I n_min
Minimum eligible backlog needed to delegate work or acquire an SQ lease.
Zero selects the default of 16, capped at
.IR n_max .
.TP
.I rescue_us
Rescue timer interval in microseconds. Zero selects 1000; nonzero values
are clamped to the range 10 through 100000. Without preemption notifiers,
the timer interval is at most 100 microseconds.
.TP
.I features
Output feature bits enabled for this ring. The input value is ignored.
.B IORING_SPARE_FEAT_PULL
indicates that pull leases are enabled. Liburing uses this bit to select
its pull submission path. The kernel copies this field to the caller
before publishing the attachment; if that copy fails, registration fails
with
.B -EFAULT
and the ring remains unattached. The structure remains 56 bytes;
.I rescue_us
and
.I features
occupy offsets 48 and 52, respectively.
.SS Flags
.TP
.B IORING_SPARE_F_NO_SPLIT
Restrict wait-time splitting to chunks of stalled executors.
.TP
.B IORING_SPARE_F_OWNER_POST
Disable direct completion publication by executors.
.TP
.B IORING_SPARE_F_NO_ACCUMULATE
Disable accumulation of push work.
.TP
.B IORING_SPARE_F_NO_BLOCK
Accepted for compatibility; it matches the v5.14 default behavior.
.TP
.B IORING_SPARE_F_FIXED_NMIN
Keep the delegation threshold constant.
.TP
.B IORING_SPARE_F_NO_PULL
Disable pull leases and retain push delegation.
.TP
.B IORING_SPARE_F_EXEC_BLOCK
Enable blocking retries in executor context.
.TP
.B IORING_SPARE_F_EXEC_FINISH
Request the optional executor finishing path while the owner waits.
.TP
.B IORING_SPARE_F_NO_TIER
Wake executors without considering CPU tiers.
.TP
.B IORING_SPARE_F_NO_NOTIFIER
Disable preemption notifiers and use timer-based rescue.
.SS Modes
.TP
.B IORING_SPARE_MODE_AUTO (0)
Adaptively delegate eligible runs according to the available executor
capacity and pending work.
.TP
.B IORING_SPARE_MODE_ALWAYS (1)
Delegate every eligible run, waking executors as needed, subject to the
chunk limits.
.TP
.B IORING_SPARE_MODE_NEVER (2)
Keep the ring attached to the group, but never delegate SQEs. The resource
freeze described below still applies.
.SS Registration rules
The ring must have all of
.BR IORING_SETUP_SINGLE_ISSUER ,
.BR IORING_SETUP_DEFER_TASKRUN ,
and
.BR IORING_SETUP_SUBMIT_ALL
set. It must not have any of
.BR IORING_SETUP_IOPOLL ,
.BR IORING_SETUP_SQPOLL ,
.BR IORING_SETUP_CQE32 ,
.BR IORING_SETUP_SQE128 ,
.BR IORING_SETUP_SQ_REWIND ,
.BR IORING_SETUP_SQ_SHARED ,
or
.BR IORING_SETUP_CQE_MIXED
set. No BPF filter may be installed on the ring. Registration must be
performed by the ring's submitting task, as required by
.BR IORING_SETUP_SINGLE_ISSUER .
A ring already attached to a group cannot be registered again;
this fails with
.BR -EBUSY .
Invalid settings, including unsupported
.I flags
bits, fail with
.BR -EINVAL .
.PP
Pull leases additionally require
.B IORING_SETUP_NO_SQARRAY
and
.BR IORING_SETUP_TASKRUN_FLAG ,
with
.B IORING_SPARE_F_NO_PULL
clear. Otherwise registration succeeds with push delegation only and
.B IORING_SPARE_FEAT_PULL
clear. Liburing normally requests
.B IORING_SETUP_NO_SQARRAY
when creating a ring. The mode controls whether work is offered;
.B IORING_SPARE_MODE_NEVER
does not offer a lease even if the feature bit is present.
.PP
The underlying
.B IORING_REGISTER_SPARE
operation takes this structure as its argument and requires
.I nr_args
to be 1. The liburing helper supplies this value.
.SS Eligible operations
Only
.BR IORING_OP_READ ,
.BR IORING_OP_WRITE ,
.BR IORING_OP_READ_FIXED ,
and
.B IORING_OP_WRITE_FIXED
are eligible for delegation. An SQE may have
.B IOSQE_FIXED_FILE
and
.B IOSQE_ASYNC
set, but no other SQE flags, and must have zero
.I personality
and
.IR attr_type_mask .
Linked or drained SQEs, vectored I/O, and operations with indirect input
descriptors are handled by the normal submission path. Eligibility does
not change the application's obligation to keep I/O buffers valid until
completion.
.PP
The file offset must not be -1. Writes require an infinite
.B RLIMIT_FSIZE
for the library to skip submission entry. The library samples this limit
at registration. A later limit change can cause an extra kernel entry;
the kernel checks eligibility again and hands the lease back with
.B IORING_SQ_TASKRUN
set when necessary. File properties and fixed-resource validity are
checked by the kernel.
.SS Pull submission
For a pull ring, liburing publishes the SQ tail with release ordering and
reads the SQ head with acquire ordering. After publication it may skip
the submission syscall only when
.B IORING_SQ_LEASED
is set, neither
.B IORING_SQ_TASKRUN
nor
.B IORING_SQ_CQ_OVERFLOW
is set, the SQ has free space, and every unconsumed SQE is eligible.
The submitting task must be the only SQ producer. Published SQEs must
remain unchanged until the SQ head passes them; I/O buffers remain valid
until completion.
.PP
The submitted count is the published SQ tail minus the head observed by
the library. It may include SQEs still pending from an earlier call.
If entry is skipped, the submission helper returns the submitted count.
If waiting still requires entry, liburing enters with zero submissions
and
.BR IORING_ENTER_GETEVENTS ;
it returns a negative error or, on success, the submitted count. When
liburing enters with a nonzero submission count, it returns the kernel's
submission result, including short results. This accounting also applies
to the timeout and registered-wait submission helpers. A raw zero-submit
entry returns zero. For pull rings, a raw nonzero submission entry also
accounts for SQEs already consumed by the lessee; it may still return
short or
.B -EAGAIN
if the owner cannot allocate requests for remaining work.
.SS Resource freeze
While attached, fixed file and buffer tables cannot change
.RB ( -EBUSY ).
Register fixed files and buffers before attaching the ring, even in
.BR IORING_SPARE_MODE_NEVER .
The freeze covers registering, unregistering, updating, and cloning into
these tables, changing the fixed file allocation range, and registering a
BPF filter. It also covers operations that install or remove direct file
descriptors, including incoming
.B IORING_MSG_SEND_FD
messages, and kernel buffer registration and unregistration.
.PP
.BR io_uring_unregister_spare (3)
detaches the ring from its group. The resource freeze persists after
detachment while any delegated chunk remains outstanding. Drive and drain
outstanding completions before changing the tables; such changes can
continue to return
.B -EBUSY
until the chunks have been retired.
.PP
The underlying
.B IORING_UNREGISTER_SPARE
operation requires a NULL argument and
.I nr_args
of 0. The liburing helper supplies these values.
.SS Debug operation
.BR io_uring_register_spare_debug (3)
passes the in/out
.I dbg
argument to
.B IORING_REGISTER_SPARE_DEBUG
(opcode 40), with
.I nr_args
equal to 1. The kernel must have
.B CONFIG_IO_URING_SPARE_DEBUG
enabled; otherwise the operation returns
.BR -EINVAL .
The 32-byte
.B io_uring_spare_debug
structure contains 32-bit
.IR point ,
.IR action ,
.IR count ,
.IR usec ,
.IR slot ,
and output
.I hits
fields, followed by a 64-bit
.I resv
field that must be zero. Points and actions are defined by
.B enum io_uring_spare_dbg_point
and
.BR enum io_uring_spare_dbg_action .
Use
.B IORING_SPARE_DBG_QUERY
to inspect a point,
.B IORING_SPARE_DBG_RELEASE
to release a parked executor, and
.B IORING_SPARE_DBG_DISARM
to disarm it. An arm action fires at most
.I count
times. A zero
.I usec
parks an executor until release, subject to the kernel's 10-second cap;
owner-side parking requires a nonzero duration. Debug controls must be
issued by the ring's submitting task.
.SH RETURN VALUE
On success, these functions return 0. On failure, they return a negative
error code.
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B -EINVAL
The kernel does not implement SpareRing, the ring is incompatible, or the
registration arguments are invalid.
.TP
.B -EOPNOTSUPP
The kernel does not support the requested SpareRing operation.
.TP
.B -EBUSY
The ring is already attached to a group, or outstanding work prevents
the requested change.
.TP
.B -EPERM
The executor group named by
.I attach_fd
belongs to a different thread group.
.TP
.B -ENOMEM
Insufficient memory to create the executor group or attachment.
.TP
.B -EFAULT
An argument or CPU bitmap address is invalid, or the feature output is
not writable.
.SH EXAMPLES
.in +4n
.EX
struct io_uring ring;
struct io_uring_spare_reg reg = {
	.attach_fd = -1,
	.nr_exec = 2,
	.mode = IORING_SPARE_MODE_ALWAYS,
};
unsigned int flags = IORING_SETUP_SINGLE_ISSUER |
		     IORING_SETUP_DEFER_TASKRUN |
		     IORING_SETUP_SUBMIT_ALL |
		     IORING_SETUP_TASKRUN_FLAG;
int ret;

ret = io_uring_queue_init(256, &ring, flags);
if (ret)
	return ret;
/* Register any fixed files and buffers here, before attaching. */
ret = io_uring_register_spare(&ring, &reg);
if (ret) {
	io_uring_queue_exit(&ring);
	return ret;
}
/* Submit I/O and consume completions here. */
ret = io_uring_unregister_spare(&ring);
/* Drain outstanding I/O before changing fixed resource tables. */
io_uring_queue_exit(&ring);
return ret;
.EE
.in
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR io_uring_setup (2),
.BR io_uring_register (2),
.BR io_uring_register_files (3),
.BR io_uring_register_buffers (3),
.BR io_uring_submit (3)
